#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:1
#: 1c92ab77193a457e95cf97b6af3b31b1
msgid "Malmquist Productivity and Reference Information"
msgstr "Malmquist 生产率与参照信息"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:3
#: a510aec68e2649f594536f78a8707b76
msgid ""
"A hospital can be efficient in every year and still fail to improve its "
"productivity. Another hospital can remain behind the leaders yet make "
"substantial progress. These statements are not contradictory. Efficiency "
"describes an organization's position relative to a benchmark at one point"
" in time; productivity change asks whether its input--output performance "
"improved between two points in time. Managers need both pieces of "
"information because they lead to different conversations. A persistent "
"operating shortfall calls for attention to implementation, while a change"
" in the sector's best-observed possibilities raises questions about "
"investment, organization, regulation, and the diffusion of practice."
msgstr "一家医院可以每年都有效率，却始终没有提高生产率；另一家医院可以一直落后于领先者，却取得显著进步。这两种说法并不矛盾。效率描述组织在某一时点相对于标杆的位置，生产率变化则考察其投入—产出绩效在两个时点之间是否改善。管理者需要同时掌握这两类信息，因为它们引向不同的讨论：持续的经营缺口要求关注执行，而行业最佳观测生产机会的变化则引出投资、组织、监管和实践扩散等问题。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:13
#: f3b8dbdbf443413985c2d578d62d1565
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The Malmquist family provides a disciplined way to organize that "
"conversation. It compares the same producer in two periods and uses DEA "
"technologies to distinguish a change in benchmark-relative operating "
"performance from a change in the production opportunities visible in the "
"data. Caves, Christensen, and Diewert developed the distance-function "
"foundation of the index {cite:p}`caves1982b`; Färe, Grosskopf, Norris, "
"and Zhang established the widely used output-oriented constant-returns "
"DEA formulation {cite:p}`fare1994`."
msgstr ""
"Malmquist 模型族为这类讨论提供了严谨框架。它比较同一生产者在两个时期的表现，并利用 DEA "
"技术区分相对标杆经营绩效的变化与数据所呈现生产机会的变化。Caves、Christensen 和 Diewert 奠定了该指数的距离函数基础 "
"{cite:p}`caves1982b`；Färe、Grosskopf、Norris 和 Zhang 建立了广泛使用的产出导向、规模报酬不变 "
"DEA 形式 {cite:p}`fare1994`。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:21
#: 556cb62e503e4f15ae4015435256a151
msgid ""
"One decision runs through every Malmquist study: **which observations are"
" allowed to define the benchmark for each comparison?** The conventional "
"adjacent-period index uses the two contemporaneous technologies. A global"
" index uses one common technology built from the full study horizon. "
"These are best understood as two reference- information policies within "
"the same productivity family. They answer closely related questions, but "
"the evidence available to the evaluator—and therefore the meaning of the "
"result—is different."
msgstr ""
"每项 Malmquist 研究都贯穿一个决策：**每次比较允许哪些观测界定标杆？** "
"传统相邻期指数使用两个同期技术；全局指数则使用由整个研究时段构造的一项共同技术。最好把二者理解为同一生产率模型族中的两种参照信息政策。它们回答密切相关的问题，但评价者能够使用的证据不同，结果含义也因此不同。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:29
#: 3e3a17c2aa9441a4b823360def4381f3
msgid ""
"Productivity change divided into a change in benchmark-relative operating"
" performance and a change in best-observed production opportunities"
msgstr "将生产率变化分为相对标杆经营绩效变化与最佳观测生产机会变化"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:34
#: 29bf55345719449287510efa2b6efb14
msgid ""
"A productivity result has two distinct managerial readings. One concerns "
"how fully an organization realizes the opportunities available in its own"
" period. The other concerns whether the study's best-observed "
"opportunities have become more or less favorable. Neither component, by "
"itself, identifies the cause of change."
msgstr "生产率结果具有两层不同的管理含义：一是组织在多大程度上实现了本期可用的生产机会；二是研究中最佳观测生产机会变得更有利还是更不利。任何一个分量都不能单独识别变化原因。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:40
#: e07c5ccc30a04be7ba9c0bd1eadb3dd8
msgid "Is a high efficiency score the same as productivity growth?"
msgstr "高效率得分是否等同于生产率增长？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:42
#: 79dedccd66bd4f39b7666bf7cc3bdc76
msgid ""
"No. Consider a clinic that lies on the estimated best-practice benchmark "
"in both 2024 and 2025. Its contemporaneous efficiency score is one in "
"both years. If the 2025 benchmark permits more treatments from the same "
"resources, the clinic has nevertheless experienced productivity growth. "
"Conversely, a clinic can reduce its shortfall from best practice while "
"the sector's observed opportunities deteriorate. Its operating "
"performance improves relative to its peers, but its overall productivity "
"need not rise."
msgstr ""
"不是。假设一家诊所 2024 年和 2025 年都位于估计的最佳实践标杆上，其同期效率得分两年均为 1。若 2025 "
"年标杆表明同样资源可以提供更多诊疗，该诊所仍然经历了生产率增长。反过来，诊所可以在行业观测生产机会恶化时缩小与最佳实践的差距：其相对同业的经营绩效改善，但总体生产率未必上升。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:50
#: 9663c1fd895740febf8fb6219901b76f
msgid ""
"To keep the two dates in a cross-period comparison distinct, let "
"$z^\\sigma=(x^\\sigma,y^\\sigma)$ denote the organization's operating "
"plan in period $\\sigma$, and let $\\mathcal T^\\tau$ denote the "
"production possibilities supported by the observations admitted to "
"reference period $\\tau$. The appraisal $d^\\tau(z^\\sigma)$ therefore "
"asks how the plan actually operated in period $\\sigma$ would perform "
"when judged by the opportunities documented in period $\\tau$. DEAPack "
"uses a common direction for reporting radial performance:"
msgstr ""
"为在跨期比较中清楚区分两个日期，令 $z^\\sigma=(x^\\sigma,y^\\sigma)$ 表示组织在时期 $\\sigma$ "
"的经营方案，令 $\\mathcal T^\\tau$ 表示获准进入参照期 $\\tau$ 的观测所支持的生产可能性。因此，评价 "
"$d^\\tau(z^\\sigma)$ 考察时期 $\\sigma$ 的实际经营方案若按时期 $\\tau$ "
"所记录的生产机会判断会有怎样的表现。DEAPack 用统一方向报告径向绩效："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:58
#: 10e985ecfded40679ae066a7e935ed9e
msgid ""
"under input orientation, $d^\\tau(z^\\sigma)$ is the Farrell input-"
"contraction factor $\\theta$;"
msgstr "投入导向下，$d^\\tau(z^\\sigma)$ 是 Farrell 投入收缩因子 $\\theta$；"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:60
#: a0bc9fb4a04b40e7af47e4f7b0638714
msgid ""
"under output orientation, it is the reciprocal, $1/\\phi$, of the Farrell"
" output-expansion factor."
msgstr "产出导向下，它是 Farrell 产出扩张因子的倒数 $1/\\phi$。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:63
#: aef0c0ba71cb42b0b41a352c6c4b0ec8
msgid ""
"For an observation assessed against a technology that contains it, "
"$0<d^\\tau(z^\\sigma)\\leq1$, and one indicates radial efficiency. This "
"convention makes the interpretation of change consistent: a ratio above "
"one records improvement. The reciprocal convention is also common in the "
"literature, so an empirical paper must state its distance direction "
"before numerical results can be compared."
msgstr ""
"当观测相对于包含自身的技术评价时，$0<d^\\tau(z^\\sigma)\\leq1$，取 1 "
"表示径向有效。该约定使变化解释保持一致：比率大于 1 表示改善。文献中也常用倒数约定，因此实证论文在比较数值结果前必须说明距离方向。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:69
#: d0549fd608e4428c9c23c16de776a428
msgid ""
"A static distance is an efficiency level. A Malmquist index is a ratio of"
" distances and therefore a change measure. It has no meaningful static "
"“efficient or inefficient” classification of its own. The neutral value "
"is one: an index above one indicates measured productivity growth, one "
"indicates no change, and a value below one indicates measured decline."
msgstr ""
"静态距离是效率水平；Malmquist 指数是距离之比，因此是变化测度。它自身没有有意义的静态“有效/无效”分类。中性值为 1：指数大于 1 "
"表示测得生产率增长，等于 1 表示没有变化，小于 1 表示测得下降。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:75
#: 31e3a26d1f84491bac1ff65f7dad54ef
msgid "Whose best practice is used to judge the two operating plans?"
msgstr "用谁的最佳实践评价两个经营方案？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:77
#: 45788bcc99e8459f8980622e69180373
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The conventional adjacent-period Malmquist index gives both neighboring "
"periods a voice. The organization has two observed plans, $z^t$ and "
"$z^{t+1}$, and the study has two contemporaneous technologies, $\\mathcal"
" T^t$ and $\\mathcal T^{t+1}$. Four benchmark evaluations are therefore "
"required."
msgstr ""
"传统相邻期 Malmquist 指数让两个相邻时期都参与评价。组织有两个观测方案 $z^t$ 和 $z^{t+1}$，研究有两个同期技术 "
"$\\mathcal T^t$ 和 $\\mathcal T^{t+1}$，因此需要四次标杆评价。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:82
#: 5a074d8a70534dc2a4f9d1e9ae9ed23b
msgid ""
"Four evaluations created by assessing each of two operating plans against"
" each of two contemporaneous reference technologies"
msgstr "把两个经营方案分别放到两个同期参照技术下评价所形成的四次评价"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:87
#: e0d2683a0f6f4053a05be56fd5baec24
msgid ""
"The four appraisals behind the adjacent-period index. The two own-period "
"evaluations describe contemporaneous operating performance. The two "
"cross-period evaluations make it possible to separate that performance "
"from a change in best-observed opportunities."
msgstr "相邻期指数背后的四次评价。两个本期评价描述同期经营绩效；两个跨期评价使该绩效能够与最佳观测生产机会变化区分开来。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:82
#: b853e654d9914c7d922023cd6d8ae4a6
msgid "Evaluation"
msgstr "评价"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:82
#: c687f3743fc1430eaa7eef1083529775
msgid "Economic question"
msgstr "经济问题"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:82
#: 1d3b37ad7cd648488ff605ff180509a2
msgid "$d^t(z^t)$"
msgstr "$d^t(z^t)$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:82
#: fd18b6800917444db33850e353add276
msgid ""
"How fully did the organization realize the opportunities documented in "
"the base period?"
msgstr "组织在多大程度上实现了基期记录的生产机会？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:82
#: 1dacc43a6907452c8f311b97c17b27a9
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$d^{t+1}(z^{t+1})$"
msgstr "$d^{t+1}(z^{t+1})$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:82
#: 16dbe224b27d4c43827f0c8af9c0ef25
msgid ""
"How fully did it realize the opportunities documented in the comparison "
"period?"
msgstr "组织在多大程度上实现了比较期记录的生产机会？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:82
#: 243dcd59a96a4808b7e9c6f4f5cf72f7
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$d^t(z^{t+1})$"
msgstr "$d^t(z^{t+1})$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:82
#: 009cbef7eb0c4ff899357ac9de4972a8
msgid ""
"How would the later operating plan be judged using the earlier "
"information set?"
msgstr "若使用较早时期的信息集，后期经营方案会得到怎样的评价？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:82
#: 5a5c37f7c54f4f4191da4a27fb943d4b
#, python-brace-format
msgid "$d^{t+1}(z^t)$"
msgstr "$d^{t+1}(z^t)$"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:82
#: 43178932bf3d4b96be06f7cf942dfc8c
msgid ""
"How would the earlier operating plan be judged using the later "
"information set?"
msgstr "若使用较晚时期的信息集，早期经营方案会得到怎样的评价？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:99
#: 80540294b9d54332bf737bcff141d298
msgid ""
"Holding the base-period technology fixed produces one assessment of "
"productivity change:"
msgstr "固定基期技术，得到一种生产率变化评价："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:102
#: 98e75bf0e8b94c2b98fce8979f8912b5
msgid ""
"\n"
"M^t(z^t,z^{t+1})\n"
"=\\frac{d^t(z^{t+1})}{d^t(z^t)}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"M^t(z^t,z^{t+1})\n"
"=\\frac{d^t(z^{t+1})}{d^t(z^t)}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:107
#: 4f53852967514c03862a378f8205b2b0
msgid "Holding the comparison-period technology fixed produces another:"
msgstr "固定比较期技术，得到另一种评价："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:109
#: 68190cdd79964a4b87b64473c0da1dad
msgid ""
"\n"
"M^{t+1}(z^t,z^{t+1})\n"
"=\\frac{d^{t+1}(z^{t+1})}{d^{t+1}(z^t)}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"M^{t+1}(z^t,z^{t+1})\n"
"=\\frac{d^{t+1}(z^{t+1})}{d^{t+1}(z^t)}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:114
#: 32ebe0e7094c4ef7b23529ceaa3bc0df
msgid ""
"Neither year is automatically the more legitimate judge. The conventional"
" index gives the two assessments equal proportional weight through their "
"geometric mean:"
msgstr "没有理由自动把任何一年视为更合法的裁判。传统指数通过几何平均赋予两个评价相同的比例权重："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:117
#: db7d12df48384fadab7adbe129d7789a
msgid ""
"\n"
"M^{t,t+1}\n"
"=\\left[\n"
"\\frac{d^t(z^{t+1})}{d^t(z^t)}\n"
"\\frac{d^{t+1}(z^{t+1})}{d^{t+1}(z^t)}\n"
"\\right]^{1/2}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"M^{t,t+1}\n"
"=\\left[\n"
"\\frac{d^t(z^{t+1})}{d^t(z^t)}\n"
"\\frac{d^{t+1}(z^{t+1})}{d^{t+1}(z^t)}\n"
"\\right]^{1/2}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:125
#: 0dc6f788ef9e47519d5bbf86cd589b14
msgid ""
"The geometric mean is part of the economic comparison, not a device for "
"hiding two disagreeing results. Analysts should inspect the underlying "
"evaluations when the overall index is surprising. A marked difference "
"between the two fixed-benchmark ratios often signals substantial change "
"in the reference opportunities, weak overlap between the period samples, "
"or an influential observation."
msgstr "几何平均是经济比较的一部分，不是掩盖两个结果不一致的技巧。若总体指数出人意料，分析者应检查底层评价。两个固定标杆比率明显不同，往往意味着参照生产机会大幅变化、两期样本重叠较弱，或某个观测具有较大影响。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:131
#: ebb75a8e4cd44e4a896f0cee0ae2d016
msgid "Did the organization improve, or did best-observed opportunities change?"
msgstr "是组织改善了，还是最佳观测生产机会发生了变化？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:133
#: 539116801c5b4bdb87ea2bf8cc5aee15
msgid ""
"The classic two-part decomposition divides measured productivity change "
"into efficiency change and technical change. Efficiency change is"
msgstr "经典两分量分解把测得生产率变化分为技术效率变化与技术变动。技术效率变化为"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:136
#: d0390d5c753e4eb99ac0c06c7797b35a
msgid ""
"\n"
"EC^{t,t+1}\n"
"=\\frac{d^{t+1}(z^{t+1})}{d^t(z^t)}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"EC^{t,t+1}\n"
"=\\frac{d^{t+1}(z^{t+1})}{d^t(z^t)}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:141
#: bf53e1672ce24e858778a426507863cf
msgid ""
"It compares how fully the organization realizes the production "
"opportunities available in its own period. When $EC>1$, the measured "
"operating shortfall has narrowed relative to contemporaneous best "
"practice; when $EC<1$, it has widened. The traditional word *catch-up* "
"describes this change in relative performance, but should not be mistaken"
" for an explanation of the organizational process that produced it. "
"Better scheduling, staff learning, lower downtime, a changed case mix, "
"revised records, or a different comparison population could all move the "
"component. DEA alone cannot decide among them; distinguishing the "
"explanations requires operational and causal evidence."
msgstr ""
"它比较组织在多大程度上实现了自身时期可用的生产机会。$EC>1$ 表示相对于同期最佳实践的经营缺口缩小，$EC<1$ "
"表示缺口扩大。传统术语“追赶”描述这种相对绩效变化，却不能被误当成产生变化的组织过程解释。排班改善、员工学习、停机减少、病例组合改变、记录修订或比较总体变化都可能移动该分量。DEA"
" 本身无法在这些解释中作出选择；区分原因需要经营与因果证据。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:150
#: c08fb0ecef50427c85b1fd4bf92f8bac
msgid "The remaining component is conventionally called technical change:"
msgstr "另一个分量通常称为技术变动："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:152
#: f50e356810984ce594dfc18364baffcb
msgid ""
"\n"
"TC^{t,t+1}\n"
"=\\left[\n"
"\\frac{d^t(z^{t+1})}{d^{t+1}(z^{t+1})}\n"
"\\frac{d^t(z^t)}{d^{t+1}(z^t)}\n"
"\\right]^{1/2}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"TC^{t,t+1}\n"
"=\\left[\n"
"\\frac{d^t(z^{t+1})}{d^{t+1}(z^{t+1})}\n"
"\\frac{d^t(z^t)}{d^{t+1}(z^t)}\n"
"\\right]^{1/2}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:160
#: da9225ff126946279c0386c422d2ebf5
msgid ""
"It describes whether the best observed combinations of resources and "
"outputs became more favorable around the organization's two operating "
"plans. A value above one means that comparable organizations demonstrated"
" an improved production opportunity for this comparison. It does not show"
" that every service line advanced, nor does it prove invention or "
"technology adoption. New equipment, regulation, demand conditions, "
"organizational redesign, data coverage, and sampling variation can all "
"influence the estimated component."
msgstr ""
"它描述组织两个经营方案附近的最佳观测资源—产出组合是否变得更有利。取值大于 1 "
"表示在这次比较中，可比组织展示了改善的生产机会；它不表明每条服务线都有进步，也不能证明出现发明或技术采用。新设备、监管、需求条件、组织重构、数据覆盖和抽样变化都可能影响估计分量。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:168
#: 7b11e738bfff4174b5965e7f55b47522
msgid ""
"The qualification “for this comparison” matters. Production opportunities"
" can improve for one service mix while remaining unchanged, or even "
"becoming less favorable, for another. A hospital specializing in elective"
" procedures and an emergency hospital may therefore receive different "
"opportunity-change factors from the same pair of annual technologies. The"
" component is evaluated around each organization's operating plans; it is"
" not a single sector-wide rate that can be attached to every producer. A "
"group summary should preserve that heterogeneity rather than describe the"
" mean component as if the entire frontier had shifted uniformly."
msgstr "“在这次比较中”这一限定十分重要。生产机会可能对某种服务组合改善，却对另一组合不变甚至变差。因此，专做择期手术的医院与急诊医院即使面对同一对年度技术，也可能得到不同的机会变化因子。该分量是在各组织的经营方案附近评价的，不是可附加到所有生产者身上的单一行业变化率。群组汇总应保留这种异质性，不能把平均分量描述成整条前沿均匀移动。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:177
#: e8a43c404a354ba495d6e33ce17c720b
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Nor does an average of organization-level indexes automatically become an"
" industry productivity measure. An industry account must say how "
"organizations are weighted and how entry, exit, and movements of activity"
" or resources among them are treated. Under such an account, shifting "
"activity toward more productive organizations can contribute to industry "
"productivity even when it is not an improvement within any one continuing"
" organization. The indexes in this chapter describe organization-level "
"change; their mean does not separately identify that reallocation "
"contribution {cite:p}`foster2001aggregate`."
msgstr ""
"组织层面指数的平均值也不会自动成为行业生产率测度。行业账户必须说明组织权重，以及如何处理进入、退出和组织间活动或资源转移。在这类账户中，即使任何持续经营组织内部都没有改善，把活动转向生产率更高的组织也可能提高行业生产率。本章指数描述组织层面变化；其均值不能单独识别这种再配置贡献"
" {cite:p}`foster2001aggregate`。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:186
#: 6f0441a44a944801b590743920aa31bd
msgid ""
"For the classic output-oriented constant-returns construction, the "
"account closes exactly:"
msgstr "对经典产出导向、规模报酬不变构造而言，账户精确闭合："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:189
#: 0b1c8613d64246d2b56c3f0ecc9ef32e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"M^{t,t+1}=EC^{t,t+1}\\,TC^{t,t+1}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"M^{t,t+1}=EC^{t,t+1}\\,TC^{t,t+1}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:193
#: 49c3d6fab37248c59085182cfd5d2939
msgid ""
"This identity is useful both substantively and computationally. It tells "
"the reader how the overall change is allocated and gives the analyst a "
"basic audit: the reported components should reconstruct the index before "
"rounding. The two factors are an accounting decomposition, not estimates "
"of separate causal effects. In particular, $EC$ should not be relabelled "
"“management quality,” and $TC$ should not be relabelled “innovation” "
"without independent evidence."
msgstr ""
"该恒等式在实质和计算上都很有用：它说明总体变化如何分配，也提供基本审计——四舍五入前，报告分量应能重构指数。两个因子是会计分解，不是相互独立的因果效应估计。特别是，没有独立证据时，不能把"
" $EC$ 改称“管理质量”，也不能把 $TC$ 改称“创新”。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:200
#: 0d0bc9c36d014e379375edec37a44a90
msgid ""
"Nor does this two-part account contain an implicit decomposition of "
"scale, input mix, output mix, or allocative performance. Those are "
"different economic questions that require additional definitions and "
"maintained assumptions. A variable-returns run is informative as a "
"sensitivity analysis, but it does not automatically turn the two "
"components above into a complete scale-and-mix ledger."
msgstr "这一两分量账户也不隐含规模、投入组合、产出组合或配置绩效分解。那些是不同的经济问题，需要新增定义与维持假设。规模报酬可变结果可作为有用的敏感性分析，却不会自动把上述两个分量变成完整的规模—组合账户。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:206
#: 0020e2071a384888b5f736b71233cf12
msgid "What if one period's benchmark cannot assess the other period's plan?"
msgstr "如果一个时期的标杆无法评价另一时期的方案怎么办？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:208
#: 1af9d75134ba4cffb8577af979e879a5
msgid ""
"The two cross-period evaluations ask demanding counterfactual questions. "
"An operating plan observed in 2025 is not necessarily reproducible within"
" the opportunities represented by the 2024 sample, and the reverse "
"comparison can also be problematic. A cross-period efficiency-form "
"distance may exceed one because the evaluated plan outperforms the "
"comparison technology. Under some non-constant-returns or otherwise "
"restricted empirical technologies, the linear program may instead be "
"infeasible. These outcomes reveal something about the comparison; they "
"are not interchangeable with numerical failure."
msgstr ""
"两次跨期评价提出了要求很高的反事实问题。2025 年观测到的经营方案不一定能由 2024 "
"年样本所代表的机会再现，反向比较也可能有问题。跨期效率形式距离可能大于 "
"1，因为被评价方案超越了比较技术；在某些非规模报酬不变或其他受限经验技术下，线性规划也可能不可行。这些结果揭示了比较的性质，不能与数值求解失败混为一谈。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:217
#: 400daeaed9854254ba643984ed150c37
msgid ""
"An analyst should not replace a missing cross-period evaluation with "
"whichever one-sided ratio happens to be available. Doing so silently "
"defines a different index and destroys the stated two-benchmark account. "
"The defensible responses are to report the affected transition, "
"reconsider whether the period technologies and data are comparable, or "
"adopt a different reference-information policy for a reason stated in "
"advance."
msgstr "分析者不能用恰好可得的某个单边比率替代缺失的跨期评价。这样会暗中定义另一个指数，并破坏已声明的双标杆账户。合理做法是报告受影响的转变、重新审视各期技术和数据是否可比，或者基于事先说明的理由采用另一种参照信息政策。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:224
#: 1bd13a6f25f9480396bd1a595093d9fd
msgid ""
"This is where the global policy becomes useful. It avoids direct “new "
"plan against old technology” and “old plan against new technology” "
"programs by evaluating both plans against one encompassing information "
"set. That advantage changes the question being asked; it is not a "
"numerical repair applied only to inconvenient rows."
msgstr "这正是全局政策的用处。它把两个方案放到同一个覆盖性信息集下评价，从而避免直接求解“新方案相对于旧技术”和“旧方案相对于新技术”。这一优势同时改变了研究问题；它不是只对不方便的行实施的数值修复。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:229
#: 800f353b4b5c4ef8a2f63227a1bfe2fe
msgid "Should all years share one retrospective benchmark?"
msgstr "是否应让所有年份共享一个回溯性标杆？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:231
#: 34e2c361c8b046ec8b5609454e0e486e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For a long-horizon assessment, a ministry or corporate group may want "
"every year's performance expressed against the same body of observed "
"opportunities. This is a change in the **reference-information policy**, "
"not a new substantive theory of productivity. Let $\\mathcal T^G$ be the "
"common technology formed from all observations in a declared study "
"horizon {cite:p}`pastor2005`, and let $d^G(z)$ be the corresponding "
"efficiency-form distance. “Global” here means full-sample across time. It"
" does not mean a universal technology beyond the population and years in "
"the dataset."
msgstr ""
"在长期评价中，主管部门或企业集团可能希望用同一套观测生产机会表达每一年的绩效。这是**参照信息政策**的变化，不是新的生产率实质理论。令 "
"$\\mathcal T^G$ 表示由已声明研究时段内全部观测形成的共同技术 {cite:p}`pastor2005`，$d^G(z)$ "
"为相应效率形式距离。此处“全局”指跨时期完整样本，不表示超越数据中总体和年份的普适技术。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: 871d3638d6ac42e6b1a8eae03a4f3baa
msgid ""
"Contemporaneous period-specific and full-horizon global reference "
"information policies across three periods"
msgstr "三个时期的同期分期参照信息政策与覆盖全时段的全局参照信息政策"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:244
#: fadffe1e15bc454da825bf38ab11ae4c
msgid ""
"Reference technologies encode an information policy. A contemporaneous "
"benchmark uses only practices observed in one period. A global benchmark "
"admits the complete study horizon. The choice determines which observed "
"practices can define best practice and therefore what the measured change"
" means."
msgstr "参照技术体现一种信息政策。同期标杆只使用某一时期观测到的实践；全局标杆允许使用完整研究时段。该选择决定哪些观测实践可以界定最佳实践，也因此决定测得变化的含义。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:250
#: 1737077b7a2e487ea4055dc4602ed839
msgid "With one common benchmark, the sensitivity comparison is a direct ratio:"
msgstr "使用一个共同标杆时，敏感性比较是一个直接比率："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:252
#: 8e99df32432346f1843c7efd04c96c15
msgid ""
"\n"
"GM^{t,t+1}=\\frac{d^G(z^{t+1})}{d^G(z^t)}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"GM^{t,t+1}=\\frac{d^G(z^{t+1})}{d^G(z^t)}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:256
#: 2a1f06d451c24221af77f0c7d58ca810
msgid ""
"The direction is unchanged: $GM>1$ indicates improvement. Because the "
"same information set judges both plans, no geometric mean across two "
"annual technologies is needed. The common reference also avoids asking "
"whether the later plan can be represented by the earlier technology, and "
"vice versa. It therefore avoids the two off-diagonal programs that can "
"make the adjacent-period index infeasible. That is a consequence of the "
"declared information policy, not a row-by-row repair for troublesome "
"results."
msgstr ""
"方向保持不变：$GM>1$ "
"表示改善。由于两个方案由同一信息集评价，不需要再对两个年度技术取几何平均。共同参照也避免询问后期方案能否由早期技术表示以及反向问题，因此避开了可能使相邻期指数不可行的两个非对角规划。这是声明的信息政策产生的结果，不是逐行修复棘手结果。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:263
#: c6513b019f2f45b3b2dea4ae56d5acf9
msgid "The choice should follow the reporting purpose:"
msgstr "选择应服从报告目的："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: 2daa9294ac4f49128f36ff3487729b8d
msgid "Reporting concern"
msgstr "报告关注点"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: e508dae649d249e285d09c1a58bda95a
msgid "Two contemporaneous technologies"
msgstr "两个同期技术"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: 9039f1d2f92b452092eae1e8f2659e96
msgid "One global technology"
msgstr "一个全局技术"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: 373a5ee7d4cf4f968a17b32e6ee78601
msgid "Central question"
msgstr "核心问题"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: 08bad5aba41047dfa25b4ede1c646832
msgid ""
"How did performance change when each neighboring year contributes its own"
" benchmark?"
msgstr "当两个相邻年度分别贡献自身标杆时，绩效如何变化？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: 717b0c9d57094754a463828ff1118ad2
msgid "How did performance change relative to one full-horizon benchmark?"
msgstr "相对于一个覆盖全时段的标杆，绩效如何变化？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: 757a57bfca2a439e80274dffd14d502f
msgid "Information admitted"
msgstr "纳入的信息"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: 35212329f2d5450faa1dd0007b48c751
msgid "The two relevant period samples"
msgstr "两个相关时期的样本"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: d58f4e4e1e2f4a47b945ccafbd6a5c9c
msgid "All periods in the declared study horizon"
msgstr "已声明研究时段的全部时期"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: b0c66a6121da47e18d91bc55ab429832
msgid "Cross-period assessment"
msgstr "跨期评价"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: 913a1d80c1374a2ca32700f220e98c72
msgid "Required"
msgstr "需要"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: e06eeabbdc3c4dc292565ba312d35aca
msgid "Not required"
msgstr "不需要"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: 8705f9a6652744778097985866b4c895
msgid "Long-run chaining"
msgstr "长期链接"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: cbd0e8e4aa45487b8f4a928d38dfd8ca
msgid "Generally path dependent"
msgstr "通常具有路径依赖"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: 00ec302fe67a4ab19840f6615d08285b
msgid "Circular within a fixed global sample"
msgstr "在固定全局样本内满足循环一致性"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: f9eb9a67c789458292ca20691dc15872
msgid "Revision when later years arrive"
msgstr "新增后期年份时的修订"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: 9ccf258b7ade43f393b8db3641744522
msgid "Mainly through affected period technologies"
msgstr "主要通过受影响时期的技术"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:239
#: f446ff59d893496e8fa0810e3f71184f
msgid "Potentially all historical global distances"
msgstr "可能修订全部历史全局距离"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:273
#: 0a87e097b88940f8b5e41155d82ba3a0
msgid ""
"Neither policy is universally superior. The adjacent account is natural "
"when each year's institutional environment deserves separate standing. "
"The common reference is useful when a board wants one retrospective "
"yardstick and internally consistent long-run chaining. A short comparison"
" of the two is often an informative sensitivity check; it should not "
"become a second parallel analysis with identically named components."
msgstr "两种政策都不是普遍更优。若每一年度的制度环境应当分别拥有评价地位，相邻期账户很自然；若董事会需要一个回溯性共同尺度和内部一致的长期链接，共同参照很有用。简短比较二者通常是有信息价值的敏感性检查，但不应发展成使用相同分量名称的第二套平行分析。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:280
#: 1b93a65baeb542a783fb317f8097e32b
msgid "What does circularity buy, and what does it cost?"
msgstr "循环一致性带来什么，又付出什么代价？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:282
#: 2d900cbc25344764aad80f0d726c0e95
msgid "Suppose the same fixed global technology is used for three periods. Then"
msgstr "假设三个时期使用同一个固定全局技术，则"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:284
#: 794f5f5bb66e42f3ad7938b243da82dd
msgid ""
"\n"
"GM^{t,t+1}GM^{t+1,t+2}\n"
"=\\frac{d^G(z^{t+1})}{d^G(z^t)}\n"
" \\frac{d^G(z^{t+2})}{d^G(z^{t+1})}\n"
"=GM^{t,t+2}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"GM^{t,t+1}GM^{t+1,t+2}\n"
"=\\frac{d^G(z^{t+1})}{d^G(z^t)}\n"
" \\frac{d^G(z^{t+2})}{d^G(z^{t+1})}\n"
"=GM^{t,t+2}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:291
#: 4de9a02a8d3941d092c7ce900583717f
msgid ""
"Adjacent changes compound to the same first-to-last change because the "
"intermediate distance cancels. This circularity is valuable in dashboards"
" and historical accounts: the cumulative number does not depend on which "
"intermediate reporting dates were inserted."
msgstr "相邻变化复合后等于同一首末时期变化，因为中间距离相互抵消。这种循环一致性对仪表板和历史账户很有价值：累计数值不依赖插入了哪些中间报告日期。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:296
#: b7b0f0a1735b4859ba857a972efab195
msgid ""
"But the qualifier “same fixed global technology” is crucial. A 2020--2025"
" study and a 2020--2026 study do not use the same information set. If the"
" 2026 observations reveal stronger production possibilities, earlier "
"global distances—and hence earlier productivity changes—may be revised. "
"The global index is retrospective. A result computed with observations "
"from the future relative to the evaluated year should not be presented as"
" information that managers possessed at that time."
msgstr ""
"但“同一个固定全局技术”这一限定至关重要。2020--2025 年研究与 2020--2026 年研究不使用同一信息集。若 2026 "
"年观测揭示更强生产可能性，早期全局距离乃至早期生产率变化都可能修订。全局指数具有回溯性；使用相对于被评价年份而言的未来观测所得结果，不能说成当时管理者已经拥有的信息。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:303
#: df5079f2b5a44e5ab2a09e6df357f26d
msgid ""
"This creates a practical governance choice. An operational monitoring "
"system can fix and archive each benchmark vintage, while a retrospective "
"study can recompute the history using the latest full sample. Every "
"common-reference result should therefore identify the study horizon and "
"benchmark vintage. Circularity within a vintage does not imply invariance"
" when the vintage changes."
msgstr "这形成一项实际治理选择：经营监测系统可以冻结并归档每版标杆，回溯研究则可用最新完整样本重算历史。因此，每项共同参照结果都应标明研究时段与标杆版本。同一版本内部的循环一致性不表示版本变化时仍保持不变。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:309
#: 0de0e84f48df428e9da3c79d53ddc682
msgid "Should the report show every possible time horizon?"
msgstr "报告是否应展示所有可能的时间跨度？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:311
#: 1026c398f50f4a38bf818ee1efacda55
msgid ""
"A board may want more than annual movements. It may ask whether a five-"
"year transformation agrees with the story told by the intervening annual "
"reports, or whether a disruption was temporary. Under one fixed global "
"vintage, that is a legitimate direct comparison: the first and last "
"operating plans are judged by the same retrospective production "
"benchmark. The endpoint is not a new model, and it does not attribute "
"change to events between the dates. It is another reporting horizon for "
"the same production account."
msgstr "董事会可能不只关心年度变化，还会询问五年转型是否与期间年度报告的叙事一致，或某次冲击是否只是暂时的。在一个固定全局版本下，可以合法作直接比较：首末经营方案由同一回溯性生产标杆评价。端点比较不是新模型，也不把变化归因于两个日期之间发生的事件；它只是同一生产账户的另一报告跨度。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:319
#: 143faecd4db942d88bad69f442bcaba5
msgid ""
"DEAPack therefore keeps consecutive comparisons as the default and makes "
"broader reporting deliberate. `comparison_pairs=\"all\"` returns every "
"forward date pair; an explicit selection such as `((2020, 2025),)` "
"returns only the requested horizon. The latter is usually preferable for "
"an executive figure because the base date cannot be mistaken for another "
"starting point."
msgstr ""
"因此，DEAPack 默认保留连续期比较，并要求明确选择更宽报告跨度。`comparison_pairs=\"all\"` "
"返回所有正序日期对；显式选择如 `((2020, 2025),)` "
"则只返回所需跨度。对管理层图表而言，后者通常更好，因为不会把基期误认成另一个起点。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:335
#: e131e228e4254b67ae4a343880ad9734
msgid ""
"The convenience has a visible reporting cost. With $D$ organizations and "
"$P$ dates, the complete table contains $DP(P-1)/2$ rows rather than "
"$D(P-1)$. The underlying distance evidence is reused: each operating plan"
" needs at most one own-period and one global appraisal, so the solve "
"graph remains proportional to $DP$. Yet tables, diagnostics, and "
"disclosed peers still grow with the number of pairs. All-horizon output "
"is therefore an opt-in research table, not a harmless default dashboard."
msgstr ""
"便利性也有可见的报告成本。若有 $D$ 个组织和 $P$ 个日期，完整表包含 $DP(P-1)/2$ 行，而不是 $D(P-1)$ "
"行。底层距离证据得到复用：每个经营方案最多只需一次本期评价和一次全局评价，因此求解图仍与 $DP$ "
"成比例。但表格、诊断和披露的参照单元数量仍随日期对增加。全跨度输出因此是主动选择的研究表，不应成为看似无害的默认仪表板。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:342
#: 17d81a9ddd9b4f69a2beb84e8c681981
msgid ""
"Matching is also a horizon-specific question. If a hospital is present in"
" 2020 and 2021 but not 2025, it can receive the first annual change but "
"not the five-year one. With `unbalanced=\"drop\"`, only that requested "
"change row is omitted; its valid observations still help define the "
"common benchmark. With `\"raise\"`, the selected pair is rejected so that"
" the missing institutional history must be resolved explicitly."
msgstr ""
"匹配也是与跨度有关的问题。若医院出现在 2020、2021 年而不在 2025 "
"年，它可以得到第一个年度变化，却不能得到五年变化。`unbalanced=\"drop\"` "
"只省略所请求的那一行变化，其有效观测仍可帮助界定共同标杆；`\"raise\"` 则拒绝所选日期对，要求显式处理缺失的机构历史。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:348
#: b286e896930744c9afb4a227d0d9156e
msgid ""
"When every pair has been fitted, a chart should still communicate one "
"horizon at a time. Filter both dates for a table, or fit a single "
"explicit pair before plotting. Otherwise several changes ending in 2025 "
"may appear under one comparison-year label even though they began in "
"different years."
msgstr ""
"即使已经拟合全部日期对，图表仍应一次只传达一个跨度。表格同时筛选两个日期，或者绘图前只拟合一个明确日期对。否则，若干终止于 2025 "
"年、却始于不同年份的变化可能都显示在同一个比较期标签下。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:353
#: 20a334cadc7141e79bbddca7bbb9ed2d
msgid "Who must be observed twice, and who may still shape the benchmark?"
msgstr "谁必须观测两次，谁仍可参与塑造标杆？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:355
#: 1503c6c0b6b24cd9983098881dceee42
msgid ""
"Productivity change belongs to an identified organization observed in "
"both periods. Rows must be matched by the pair `(organization, period)`, "
"never by their order in a spreadsheet. If a provider appears only in "
"2024, it cannot have a 2024--2025 change score. That does not mean its "
"2024 operation is devoid of technological information."
msgstr ""
"生产率变化属于两个时期都能识别到的同一组织。数据行必须按 `(organization, period)` "
"配对，绝不能按电子表格中的行序匹配。若服务机构只在 2024 年出现，就不能获得 2024--2025 年变化得分，但这不表示其 2024 "
"年经营活动不包含技术信息。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:360
#: 9fd237db917e4204a186d875a682ef03
msgid ""
"The **matched transition population** and the **frontier reference "
"population** should therefore be kept distinct. The former contains "
"organizations observed in both relevant periods. The latter can include "
"every valid observation admitted by the study design, including an "
"organization seen in only one period. Deleting unmatched organizations "
"merely to create a rectangular panel may move a contemporaneous or global"
" benchmark and alter the results of organizations that remain."
msgstr "因此，必须区分**匹配转变总体**与**前沿参照总体**。前者包含在两个相关时期都有观测的组织；后者可以包含研究设计允许的全部有效观测，包括只在一个时期出现的组织。仅为构造矩形面板而删除未匹配组织，可能移动同期或全局标杆，并改变保留组织的结果。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:367
#: 2a7f905b7fe74e429910a1da0d6b3ab1
msgid ""
"This distinction matters especially under a global policy. A new entrant "
"may not have its own earlier transition, yet its observed practice can "
"reshape the common benchmark for every year. The empirical report should "
"state how unmatched identities were handled, which observations formed "
"each reference technology, and whether entry and exit are themselves part"
" of the phenomenon under study."
msgstr "这一区别在全局政策下尤其重要。新进入者虽然没有自己的早期转变，却可能重塑每一年共同标杆。实证报告应说明未匹配身份如何处理、哪些观测形成各参照技术，以及进入和退出本身是否属于研究现象。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:373
#: e99b8356c6224a9ca54970191b703808
msgid "Make the benchmark choice visible"
msgstr "让标杆选择清晰可见"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:375
#: 40f5fd2109f84353ae73a130543dbcea
msgid ""
"The project-authored `multiperiod_trajectory_contrast` data provide a "
"compact way to see why reference policy matters. Five neutral service "
"trajectories are observed over three periods, with one resource index and"
" one service output. Some paths improve, some deteriorate, and some "
"change their relative operating position. The data are designed for "
"teaching policy contrasts rather than for reproducing a paper table."
msgstr ""
"项目自主编制的 `multiperiod_trajectory_contrast` 数据以简洁方式说明参照政策为何重要。五条中性服务轨迹各有三个时期的观测，并包含一项资源指数和一项服务产出。有的轨迹改善，有的恶化，有的相对经营位置发生变化。该数据用于讲解政策对比，而不是复现论文表格。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:382
#: 62c93980816f48f980932397c4059e0d
msgid ""
"Begin with the adjacent-period model that provides the chapter's main "
"productivity comparison:"
msgstr "先使用本章主要生产率比较所采用的相邻期模型："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:410
#: d74635dc49724ab1bac54736da186733
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Every certified row reconstructs $M^{t,t+1}=EC^{t,t+1}TC^{t,t+1}$. If a "
"required appraisal is unavailable or the decomposition fails to close, "
"the transition has no defensible productivity reading; diagnostic details"
" belong in the DEAPack Documentation. The operating-performance component"
" locates movement relative to each period's frontier, while the technical"
" component records movement in represented best-practice opportunities."
msgstr ""
"每一条通过认证的记录都可重构 $M^{t,t+1}=EC^{t,t+1}TC^{t,t+1}$。若任何必要评价不可得，或分解恒等式无法闭合，该转变就没有可辩护的生产率解释；诊断细节见 DEAPack Documentation。经营绩效分量刻画相对于各期前沿的移动，技术分量则记录所表示的最佳实践机会如何变化。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:418
#: cbb29dd666df4f73a7731e7d965fdf32
msgid "The result plot makes this core adjacent-period answer visible directly."
msgstr "结果图直接展示这一核心相邻期答案。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:429
#: 973067ed21b74f4899ddf6be2ba49e86
msgid ""
"Adjacent-period productivity change across five project-authored service "
"trajectories, shown relative to the no-change benchmark of one"
msgstr "项目自主编制的五条服务轨迹的相邻期生产率变化，以表示无变化的基准值 1 为参照"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:434
#: adc33334f10147fbb77e17c5a8b57c13
msgid ""
"The chart separates improvements, declines, and no-change cases without "
"attributing frontier-relative movement to management. Each point is "
"released only when its four-appraisal account is certified."
msgstr ""
"该图区分改善、下降和无变化情形，但不把相对于前沿的移动归因于管理行为。每个点仅在其四次评价账户通过认证后才予发布。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:439
#: 27746435e1b5462d84029dfc01d5b323
msgid ""
"As a deliberately brief sensitivity check, judge the same plans against "
"one full-horizon technology:"
msgstr "作为一项有意保持简短的敏感性检查，再依据一个覆盖整个期限的技术评价同一组方案："

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:458
#: a071e49febc94a5aae851778a251b4d6
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The global account uses one common retrospective information base. Two "
"global distances, $d^G(z^t)$ and $d^G(z^{t+1})$, form the headline "
"change. The two own-period distances retain the operating-performance "
"comparison $EC_G=d^{t+1}(z^{t+1})/d^t(z^t)$. Each global distance divided"
" by its own-period counterpart gives a best-practice gap; the change "
"between those gaps is $BPC_G$, and $GM=EC_G BPC_G$. Comparing `adjacent` "
"with `global_account` is therefore an interpretable sensitivity analysis,"
" not a race to select whichever policy gives the preferred number."
msgstr ""
"全局账户采用一个共同的回溯性信息基础。两个全局距离 $d^G(z^t)$ 与 $d^G(z^{t+1})$ 构成核心变化；两个本期距离保留经营绩效比较 $EC_G=d^{t+1}(z^{t+1})/d^t(z^t)$。每个全局距离除以相应本期距离得到最佳实践差距，两个差距之间的变化为 $BPC_G$，并有 $GM=EC_G BPC_G$。因此，比较 `adjacent` 与 `global_account` 是一项可解释的敏感性分析，而不是竞相选择能给出偏好数值的政策。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:467
#: 52c7f47450434aed9aae54ac8f3e480e
msgid ""
"Neither answer is a computational mistake. The difference shows that the "
"substantive conclusion depends on whether each annual opportunity set "
"receives its own standing or both plans are judged on one retrospective "
"information base. Constructor options, returned fields, and diagnostic "
"details belong in the separate DEAPack Documentation."
msgstr ""
"两个答案都不是计算错误。差异表明，实质结论取决于各年度机会集分别拥有评价地位，还是两个方案都由同一个回溯性信息基础评价。构造器选项、返回字段和诊断细节见独立的"
" DEAPack Documentation。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:472
#: 921fb3b2bf2a4bee8f1c96bd23ec17b9
msgid "Which modeling assumptions travel with the result?"
msgstr "哪些建模假设随结果一起成立？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:474
#: f76f7dc1effd44728518c6798781a537
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The widely used classic account is output oriented and assumes constant "
"returns to scale (CRS) {cite:p}`fare1994`. Output orientation asks how "
"much desirable output could be proportionally expanded with the observed "
"inputs. CRS permits proportional replication of observed activities and "
"makes input- and output-oriented radial indexes coincide in theory. These"
" assumptions may be reasonable for some sector-level studies, but they "
"are not harmless defaults."
msgstr ""
"广泛使用的经典账户采用产出导向和规模报酬不变（CRS）假设 "
"{cite:p}`fare1994`。产出导向考察在观测投入下合意产出可以同比例扩张多少；CRS "
"允许观测活动同比例复制，并使投入导向和产出导向径向指数在理论上重合。这些假设对某些行业层面研究可能合理，却不是无关紧要的默认项。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:481
#: 41214276812c402880fbee7cfe94c52e
msgid ""
"Variable returns to scale (VRS) restricts comparisons to a convex scale "
"range and can be appropriate when organizations cannot freely replicate "
"operations. Under VRS, input and output orientations can tell different "
"stories, and cross-period feasibility can be more fragile. A VRS "
"calculation can show whether conclusions depend on the scale "
"representation; it should be reported as such, not treated as a complete "
"decomposition into pure efficiency, scale, mix, and technical effects."
msgstr ""
"规模报酬可变（VRS）把比较限制在凸规模范围内，适用于组织不能自由复制经营活动的情形。VRS "
"下，投入与产出导向可能给出不同叙事，跨期可行性也更脆弱。VRS "
"计算可以检验结论是否依赖规模表示，但应如实报告为敏感性分析，不能当作纯效率、规模、组合和技术效应的完整分解。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:488
#: 4c23d4e590c44842ae226fc3e2758c65
msgid ""
"Reference populations also carry economic assumptions. If hospitals in "
"different regulatory regimes cannot reasonably learn from or be compared "
"with one another, a single pooled benchmark may exaggerate the "
"opportunities available to management. If quality is omitted, an apparent"
" output gain may represent faster but worse care. If capital is measured "
"only at book value, changes in valuation may appear as production change."
" The Malmquist calculation cannot repair a weak definition of inputs, "
"outputs, organizational comparability, or time."
msgstr ""
"参照总体同样承载经济假设。若不同监管制度下的医院无法合理相互学习或比较，单一合并标杆可能夸大管理者可用机会。若遗漏质量，表面产出增长可能只是服务更快却更差；若资本只按账面价值计量，估值变化可能表现为生产变化。Malmquist"
" 计算无法修复投入、产出、组织可比性或时间定义薄弱的问题。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:496
#: 033c7af1440c4ffc863dbd675b3bfb23
msgid ""
"The model in this chapter concerns desirable outputs. Pollution, adverse "
"events, and other undesirable outputs require an explicitly environmental"
" production technology, including assumptions about disposability and "
"joint production. Adding an emissions column to the ordinary desirable-"
"output matrix does not create an environmental productivity index."
msgstr "本章模型只涉及合意产出。污染、不良事件和其他非合意产出需要明确的环境生产技术，包括可处置性与联合生产假设。仅向普通合意产出矩阵增加一列排放数据，并不会产生环境生产率指数。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:502
#: 5bc93bd81ef4459898a35a7a1b4067c3
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Finally, all DEA productivity measures are sample-dependent frontier "
"estimates. Outliers, measurement error, and sampling variation can change"
" both the organization's distance and the benchmark against which it is "
"measured. Statistical procedures for Malmquist indexes address part of "
"this uncertainty {cite:p}`simar1999`; tighter numerical precision is not "
"a substitute for inference."
msgstr ""
"最后，所有 DEA 生产率测度都是依赖样本的前沿估计。离群值、测量误差和抽样变化都可能改变组织距离及其参照标杆。Malmquist "
"指数的统计程序处理部分不确定性 {cite:p}`simar1999`；更高数值精度不能替代统计推断。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:508
#: 893fa0e5b31d42938d819e1eacc2e2b9
msgid "What should a decision maker be told?"
msgstr "应向决策者说明什么？"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:510
#: 35a3e18bfd6049a08ad6a80256c4b2b1
msgid ""
"A useful report begins with the decision question, not the model's "
"acronym. It states whether the aim is a neighboring-year comparison under"
" two contemporaneous technologies or a retrospective history under one "
"full-horizon technology. It then reports the overall change beside the "
"appropriate two-part decomposition and explains the components as "
"benchmark-relative operating change and best-observed-opportunity change."
msgstr "有用的报告从决策问题而不是模型缩写开始。它先说明目标是在两个同期技术下比较相邻年度，还是在一个覆盖全时段的技术下回溯历史；随后把总体变化与相应两分量分解并列报告，并把分量解释为相对标杆经营变化和最佳观测机会变化。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:517
#: 28a16d90cd20440eb2fbedc53d525658
msgid ""
"The report should also make visible the orientation, returns to scale, "
"period order, matched transition population, frontier reference "
"population, handling of infeasible comparisons, study horizon, and—when a"
" global technology is used—benchmark vintage. These details determine "
"what information management was assumed to face. They are not software "
"footnotes."
msgstr "报告还应明确导向、规模报酬、时期顺序、匹配转变总体、前沿参照总体、不可行比较处理、研究时段，以及使用全局技术时的标杆版本。这些细节决定模型假定管理者面对哪些信息，绝非软件脚注。"

#: ../../chapters/04-productivity/malmquist-productivity-reference-information.md:523
#: 206e11657c6b4c1483e719b0b472b7a9
msgid ""
"Most importantly, the conclusion must stop where the method stops. A "
"Malmquist result can show that an organization's observed input--output "
"performance changed, that its shortfall relative to contemporaneous best "
"practice changed, and that the opportunities supported by the reference "
"data changed. It cannot, without complementary evidence, attribute those "
"changes to managerial skill, innovation, policy, competition, or "
"investment. Used with that discipline, the family turns repeated "
"efficiency scores into a coherent account of organizational progress "
"while keeping the information behind the benchmark open to scrutiny."
msgstr ""
"最重要的是，结论必须止于方法能够支持的边界。Malmquist "
"结果可以表明组织的观测投入—产出绩效发生变化、其相对于同期最佳实践的缺口发生变化，以及参照数据支持的生产机会发生变化；没有补充证据时，不能把这些变化归因于管理能力、创新、政策、竞争或投资。遵守这一边界，Malmquist"
" 模型族就能把重复效率得分转化为连贯的组织进步账户，同时让标杆背后的信息保持可审查。"
